                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "globule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f284e9c1-dd86-359a-a39d-f18ffaa93e0c",
                                        "entry_id": "6b1669c3-7a94-39fc-aa1e-e7d56afa36fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small round particle of substance; a drop."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96fa382d-3923-4472-9e7a-ff999df9f7ab",
                                                "sense_id": "f284e9c1-dd86-359a-a39d-f18ffaa93e0c",
                                                "text": "Suppoſe now that in a fair Day the Sun ſhines through a thin Cloud of ſuch globules of Water or Hail, and that the globules are all of the ſame bigneſs[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70bdf925-c08f-4863-9bb9-b2a0235b6d71",
                                                "sense_id": "f284e9c1-dd86-359a-a39d-f18ffaa93e0c",
                                                "text": "A civilized hotel is a little urban globule floating like scum on a rustic pool."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ba47d74-a8b5-4bfc-b925-50e21b4e37a8",
                                                "sense_id": "f284e9c1-dd86-359a-a39d-f18ffaa93e0c",
                                                "text": "They described the eggs as spherical in shape, highly transparent with a thin, horny egg membrane and a relatively wide perivitelline space. Each egg contained a single oil globule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "632dc961-3666-4db0-a327-da997d8c5cd2",
                                                "sense_id": "f284e9c1-dd86-359a-a39d-f18ffaa93e0c",
                                                "text": "Mature female black rockfish and newborn (inset), which sports an oil globule (arrow) - its prepacked lunch. Older moms give young a bigger starting meal, boosting the offsprings'^([sic]) growth and survival."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
